  "question": {
    "text": "Two plane mirrors are placed parallel to each other at a distance <math><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></math> as shown in the figure. The point source of light S is having wavelength equal to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math> . The light is reaching the screen (right of the source) only after reflection. For point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> to be 2nd maxima, the value of <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> . Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is an integer. Find value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>? (assume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math>)<br />\r<br />\r&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0055_32d66a9ec04f.jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 150px;\" />"
  },
